      "note": "Cardinal lexicon 0..99 for Dutch clock idioms: the literal atoms 0..19 of %spellout-cardinal, its tens rules of the exact form [>%%number-en>]<word>, the compound prefixes of %%number-en (literal for 1..3, the redirect =%spellout-cardinal=en for 4..9) and the stressed one of %spellout-cardinal-stressed. articleForms names the number words that are also the indefinite article (een): alone they are not number evidence, and as a clock hour they must end the phrase. Every other rule (negative, decimal, scale, ordinal, year) is counted as excluded."
